---
layout: article
title: Agent
description: Chat with the Appwrite Agent in the Console to inspect your project, explain issues, suggest next steps, and run approved actions.
---

Appwrite **Agent** is the AI chat built into the Appwrite Cloud Console. It helps you inspect the organization and project you are working in, answer Appwrite how-to questions, clarify ambiguous requests, and take approved actions through [Appwrite MCP](/docs/tooling/ai/mcp-servers/api).

You can open the Agent as a right-hand panel while you work, or use the dedicated fullscreen experience at `/agent`. Conversations, custom models, memory, MCP connections, and automations are stored on your Console account.

{% info title="Appwrite Cloud" %}
Agent is available on Appwrite Cloud. Self-hosted deployments do not include Appwrite Agent.
{% /info %}

# How it works {% #how-it-works %}

Each Agent turn can combine several capabilities:

1. **Context**: The Agent receives the current organization, project, page, and URL so answers match where you are in the Console.
2. **Conversation**: You chat in natural language, attach files, use voice input, stop or retry a run, and rate replies.
3. **Clarification**: When a request is ambiguous or risky, the Agent can ask structured choice, confirm, or text questions before continuing.
4. **Tools**: With [MCP](/docs/products/agent/mcp) connected, the Agent can search docs, list tools, and call Appwrite APIs on your behalf.
5. **Console actions**: The Agent can navigate the Console, open create wizards, refresh lists, show resource cards, and render usage charts in the chat.

Without MCP, the Agent still answers questions and guides you through setup. With **Appwrite MCP** connected, suggestion chips switch to action-oriented prompts such as listing databases or creating a table.

